From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WavJaby <WavJaby@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 09:44:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add x86 and x86_64 guests to the linker path translation

Native bridge libraries of an x86 or x86_64 guest reside in $LIB/$ABI
like those of the translated arches: /system/lib/x86/ and
/system/lib64/x86_64/.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Patch-Reason: upstream lists only the guest arches Berberis translates; ATL bridges same-arch bionic, and the table is compiled into the guest linker, which no launcher, loader or environment setting can extend
---
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 android_api/linker/linker_translate_path.cpp | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/android_api/linker/linker_translate_path.cpp b/android_api/linker/linker_translate_path.cpp
index 6f69645233cf6c289a9be6f3515b82e98e19b295..b4f71c616f8b9bcbfd7c5959e0a3e1d7cfe57cfc 100644
--- a/android_api/linker/linker_translate_path.cpp
+++ b/android_api/linker/linker_translate_path.cpp
@@ -55,6 +55,16 @@
   { "/system/lib64/" name, "/system/lib64/riscv64/" name }
 #define APEX_LIB(apex, name) \
   { "/apex/" apex "/lib64/" name, "/system/lib64/riscv64/" name }
+#elif defined(__i386__)
+#define SYSTEM_LIB(name) \
+  { "/system/lib/" name, "/system/lib/x86/" name }
+#define APEX_LIB(apex, name) \
+  { "/apex/" apex "/lib/" name, "/system/lib/x86/" name }
+#elif defined(__x86_64__)
+#define SYSTEM_LIB(name) \
+  { "/system/lib64/" name, "/system/lib64/x86_64/" name }
+#define APEX_LIB(apex, name) \
+  { "/apex/" apex "/lib64/" name, "/system/lib64/x86_64/" name }
 #else
 #error "Unknown guest arch"
 #endif
